route-arg0-helpers-to-harness

Lane: normalization

Unit: route-process-support-state-to-harness

ChildPatch: route-arg0-helpers-to-harness

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Keep process helper, clipboard staging and Linux sandbox bookkeeping under the selected harness while preserving their independent native behavior and isolation.

Requires: Unit:normalization/normalize-base-roots-for-processes, Unit:normalization/route-app-server-runtime-to-harness

Provides: Stage guarded per-process arg0 aliases and expose only the active alias directory to permissions; persist unique clipboard PNG files under harness/clipboard with native acquisition and intermediate-file cleanup; place the one-shot prefix-rule marker and synthetic mount registry under harness while preserving symlink rejection, masking and registry cleanup.

Boundary: Base-root resolution and executor harness propagation remain with their normalization owners. Alias dispatch, clipboard acquisition and attachment lifetime, policy contents, migration rules, durable home data and unrelated filesystem permissions retain native ownership.

Verification: arg0 alias placement and active-directory tests, exact configured permission-policy projections including the active alias read grant, clipboard_png_uses_harness_staging_root, execpolicy sandbox_migration_tests, core exec_policy tests, linux-sandbox registry and sandbox tests, and daemon_sockets tests cover separated roots, bytes, one-shot behavior and isolation.


